        <type><ref refid="classbool" kindref="compound">bool</ref></type>
        <definition>bool llvm::MachineFrameInfo::StackObject::isStatepointSpillSlot</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>isStatepointSpillSlot</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::MachineFrameInfo::StackObject::isStatepointSpillSlot</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= false</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>If true, this stack slot is used to spill a value (could be deopt and/or GC related) over a statepoint. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>We know that the address of the slot can&apos;t alias any LLVM IR value. This is very similar to a Spill Slot, but is created by statepoint lowering is <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_selection_d_a_g" kindref="compound">SelectionDAG</ref>, not the register allocator. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
