      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structllvm_1_1_machine_frame_info_1_1_stack_object_1a62c626ab1278cef36c4960ed40912748" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type><ref refid="classuint8__t" kindref="compound">uint8_t</ref></type>
        <definition>uint8_t llvm::MachineFrameInfo::StackObject::StackID</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>StackID</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::MachineFrameInfo::StackObject::StackID</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Identifier for stack memory type analagous to address space. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If this is non-0, the meaning is target defined. Offsets cannot be directly compared between objects with different stack IDs. The object may not necessarily reside in the same contiguous memory block as other stack objects. Objects with differing stack IDs should not be merged or replaced substituted for each other. It is assumed a target uses consecutive, increasing stack IDs starting from 1. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
